1 0 0 1 62 730 Tm
(Technology Change Management Standard) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Version 2.4) Tj
T*
(Owner: Technology Governance) Tj
T*
(Effective Date: 2026-01-01) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Purpose and Scope) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This standard defines the mandatory controls for authorising, testing, and deploying) Tj
T*
(changes to production technology services. It applies to all production changes,) Tj
T*
(including application releases, infrastructure changes, and configuration changes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Definitions) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A "change" is any addition, modification, or removal of a production service component.) Tj
T*
(An "implementer" is the individual who performs the change. An "approver" is the) Tj
T*
(individual accountable for authorising the change.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Approval) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.1 Changes must be approved before deployment to production.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.2 The approver must be independent of the implementing engineer. A change must not be) Tj
T*
(approved by the person who implemented it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.3 Approval evidence must be recorded in the change record, including the approver) Tj
T*
(identity and the approval timestamp.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Testing and Rollback) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.1 Changes must be tested in a non-production environment before deployment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.2 A documented rollback plan must be attached to the change record before deployment.) Tj
T*
(The rollback plan must identify the steps required to restore the previous service state.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.3 Emergency changes may be deployed before formal approval, but must receive) Tj
T*
(retrospective review within two business days.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Guidance) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Teams should consider deploying during low-traffic windows where practical. This is a) Tj
T*
(recommendation and not a mandatory control.) Tj
T*
ET
